e until the recall repair is complete.  Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will replace the passenger frontal air bag inflator, free of charge.  The recall began February 4, 2019.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is V01.","park_it":true,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1413222,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V018000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":29,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2010","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2010","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2010","make":"DODGE","model":"CHALLENGER"},{"year":"2010","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2011","make":"DODGE","model":"DAKOTA"},{"year":"2013","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2012","make":"DODGE","model":"CHALLENGER"},{"year":"2010","make":"DODGE","model":"DAKOTA"},{"year":"2011","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2012","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2011","make":"DODGE","model":"CHALLENGER"},{"year":"2012","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2013","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2013","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2013","make":"DODGE","model":"CHALLENGER"},{"year":"2011","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2012","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2011","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"CHALLENGER"},{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2014","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2015","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"19V680000","received":"2019-09-26","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"SEAT BELTS:FRONT:ANCHORAGE","summary":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC) is recalling certain 2011-2018 Jeep Wrangler right hand drive vehicles.  The driver's seat belt buckle mounting strap may fracture and separate from the seat frame.","consequence":"A separated or severed seat belt buckle strap will result in an inoperable seat belt, increasing the risk of injury in the event of a crash.","remedy":"FCA US will notify owners, and dealers will replace the driver's seat belt buckle, free of charge.  Interim notices informing owners of the safety risk were mailed November 19, 2019.  Owners will received a second letter and the recall began March 26, 2020.  Owners may contact FCA customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  FCA's number for this recall is VA6.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":11463,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V680000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":8,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2013","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2011","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2012","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2015","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2017","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2016","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2018","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"16V288000","received":"2016-05-11","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"AIR BAGS:FRONTAL:DRIVER SIDE:INFLATOR MODULE","summary":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC) is recalling certain model year 2011-2016 Right Hand Drive Jeep Wrangler vehicles manufactured February 16, 2010, to May 2, 2016. The clockspring assembly may become contaminated with dust and cause the air bag circuit to fail.","consequence":"Failure of the air bag circuit may prevent the driver's frontal air bag from deploying in the event of a crash, increasing the risk of injury.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will replace the clockspring, wheel back cover, and column shroud, free of charge.  The recall began on August 11, 2016.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is S40.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":7196,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=16V288000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2013","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2011","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2012","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2015","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2016","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"14V632000","received":"2014-10-08","manufacturer":"Chrysler Group LLC","component":"TIRES:PRESSURE MONITORING AND REGULATING SYSTEMS","summary":"Chrysler Group LLC (Chrysler) is recalling certain model year 2014 Chrysler Town and Country and Dodge Grand Caravan vehicles manufactured March 20, 2014, to April 22, 2014, and 2014 Jeep Wrangler vehicles manufactured March 21, 2014, to April 22, 2014.  Due to a software error, the Tire Pressure Monitoring System (TPMS) may fail to learn the locations of the individual sensors while the vehicle is being driven.  As a result, the low tire pressure warning light will illuminate, despite the the tire pressures being within specification.  Should one of the tires lose air pressure, the driver would not be notified of the change in air pressure.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard No. 138, \"Tire Pressure Monitoring Systems.\"","consequence":"If the TPMS light illuminates because the sensors cannot be located, it could mask an actual low tire pressure condition, possibly resulting in tire failure, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Chrysler has notified owners, and dealers will reprogram the TPMS module, free of charge.  The recall began on October 23, 2014.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403. Chrysler's number for this recall is P63.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":10390,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=14V632000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":3,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"},{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"WRANGLER"},{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
